in a face to nation interview secretary  of state anthony blinken says the white  house is working 24 7 to evacuate more  people from afghanistan  that country is close to economic  collapse after the u.s withdrew and the  taliban ousted the american-backed  government for a small number of  families trying to escape civilian  evacuation flights offer a lifeline mts  tae app takes us now inside one of those  flights leaving the capital  they consider themselves the lucky ones  afghans mostly families checking in for  an evacuation flight for a chance at a  new life  just getting to this point for so many  afghans has been  extraordinarily difficult and now  they have to take the next big step in  their journey  a journey into the unknown nabi roshan  is taking with his young family  one of afghanistan's most popular  comedians he hosted a nightly tv comedy  show where no one not even the taliban  was off limits but after it sees power  in august  russian says there's little left to  laugh about do the taliban like jokes  i don't think yeah i think so  did you receive any threats yeah  who  i don't know just said  i  i will  kill you  maybe  this evacuation flight is one of over a  dozen that have been organized with  meticulous precision by the government  of qatar the tiny persian gulf kingdom  has played an oversized role in helping  more than 70 000 people flee from  afghanistan since the u.s withdrawal  nearly two months ago  it's in stark contrast to the chaos that  followed immediately after the taliban  sees power and the desperate scenes of  afghans trying to flee  some losing their lives  in one of the many paradoxes of the new  afghanistan also boarding this flight to  the qatari capital doha are senior  members of the taliban government  including the interim foreign minister  amir khan mataki who stopped to speak  exclusively to cbs news in his first  interview with the u.s network  is the taliban prepared to have full  diplomatic relationship with the united  states  he says we want a positive relationship  with the world including the us but we  will not accept the military presence of  any country we only welcome diplomatic  and economic ties  there are so many afghans on this flight  who are leaving what is your message to  afghans who want to leave  if they want to leave they can leave he  says in our government all afghans  whether they agree or disagree with our  policies are free  but after just two months in power the  taliban has already stripped away basic  freedoms including barring most women  from going to work and forbidding girls  over the age of 12 from going to school  after 20 years of war the group it seems  hasn't changed very much  which is why so many of afghanistan's  best and brightest are leaving for cbs  mornings i'm impeached at the kabul  airport
 

